## Usage

A stem from `baseline` (a number or a column, default 0) to each `y`, on either side of it, with a point at the end. Stems run along y, or along x when `y` is the categorical column (`orientation` overrides the detection); `z` places both parts in 3D. Style the stems with their `stem` object (`stem={{ color: "gray", width: 2, dash: [2, 2] }}` in Svelte, `stem={"color": "gray", "width": 2, "dash": [2, 2]}` in Python), or with `theme.marks.Lollipop.color` and `.width`. `stemColor` and `stemWidth` are removed; use `stem.color` and `stem.width`. The heads are Points, sized as Points are: `size` is a head's diameter in CSS pixels (5 by default), and the stems default to 1.5 CSS pixels wide. `size` and the head-only properties (`fill`, `shape`, `select`, `hover`, `brush`) apply to the heads, while `visible`, `opacity`, `respond`, `identity`, `enterEffect`/`exitEffect`, and the animation switches apply to both, and the mark's one legend entry toggles both.

Lollipop is a built-in template (TODO 130.3): BarGeometry places each stem's base and tip, a Segments draws the stems and Points the heads. It is importable from `hmplot/charts`; "Writing a pattern" in docs/USAGE.md has a hand-written lollipop as a worked example.
